        "title": "Stopping distance",
        "text": "With constant deceleration a, the velocity is $$v(t)=v0-a t$$, which is $$0$$ at $$t=\\frac{v0}{a}$$. The distance is the integral of v(t) from $$0$$ to $$\\frac{v0}{a}$$, which is $$\\frac{{v0}^2}{2a}$$.",
